      "part_type": "Hadith",
      "path": "/books/al-kafi:4:1:29:2",
      "text": [
        " قَالَ أَبُو عَبْدِ اللَّهِ ( عليه السلام ) مَا مِنْ مُؤْمِنٍ أَقْرَضَ مُؤْمِناً يَلْتَمِسُ بِهِ وَجْهَ اللَّهِ إِلَّا حَسَبَ اللَّهُ لَهُ أَجْرَهُ بِحِسَابِ الصَّدَقَةِ حَتَّى يَرْجِعَ إِلَيْهِ مَالُهُ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Ali Bin Ibrahim, from his father and Muhammad Bin Ismail, from Al Fazl Bin Shazaan, altogether from Ibn Abu Umeyr, from Hammad, from Rabie Bin Abdullah, from Fuzayl Bin Yasaar who said, ",
          "‘Abu Abdullah<sup>asws</sup> said: ‘There is none from a Believer who lends to a Believer, seeking by it the Face of Allah<sup>azwj</sup>, except that Allah<sup>azwj</sup> would Reckon for him his Recompense by accounting it as a charity (on his behalf) until his wealth returns to him’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "2. Ali ibn Ibrahim has narrated from his father and Muhammad ibn Isma‘il from al-Fadl ibn Shadhan, all from ibn abu ‘Umayr from Hammad from Rib’iy ibn ‘Abd Allah from Fudayl ibn Yasar who has said the following: “Abu ‘Abd Allah, ‘Alayhi al-Salam, has said, ‘For every believing person who provides a loan for another believing person, for the sake of Allah, Allah counts its reward as that of giving charity until the time the loan is paid back.’” "
        ]
      }
    },
